{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c5188f993f3252da322e811e82e58f6346c6556f70853ba9a681c525254d6fde","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar_reconciler apply layer — comment dedup seam crossing","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_dedup_seam_crossing.py","BindingStore.is_comment_mapped","_diff_comments","_record_comment_id","acli_cli_ops.add_comment","ACLI_SUCCESS_ENVELOPE","test_recorded_post_is_skipped_and_unrecorded_control_still_emits","test_inert_is_comment_mapped_reemits_the_recorded_comment"],"problem_keywords":["dedup","seam-crossing","binding store","comment mapping","invariant coverage","test isolation"],"propositions":["The dedup suite lacks end-to-end test coverage across the apply-to-differ seam because differ tests and apply tests each seed the invariant the other is supposed to establish, allowing inert guards to pass undetected.","A real envelope posted through the real recording path (_record_comment_id) against a real BindingStore and then re-diffed with _diff_comments against that same store must skip the recorded comment but still emit unrecorded control comments.","Forcing the BindingStore.is_comment_mapped guard to return False on the same store instance must cause the recorded comment to be re-emitted, proving the skip depends on the guard rather than passing vacuously."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787883324847947001,"uuid":"1fc87ff7-b76d-486f-9599-94d6526f397d"}